<BaseLayout title="Identity Partners">
  <h1>Identity Partners</h1>

  <p>
    Identity Partners exists for people who want something more human, more
    intelligent, and more structurally honest than the standard menu of helping
    professions. Not therapy. Not coaching. Not mentoring. Not consultancy. And
    not friendship.
  </p>

  <p>
    Each of those models offers something valuable — but each also carries
    structural limits. Therapy is safe but non‑reciprocal. Coaching is optimistic
    but often superficial. Mentoring is directional but hierarchical. Consultancy
    is expert but impersonal. Friendship is warm but uncontained.
  </p>

  <p>
    We work in the space between these models. Not as a blend, but as a distinct
    relational practice. We offer the psychological safety of therapy, the
    strategic clarity of consultancy, the forward energy of coaching, and the
    human warmth of genuine partnership — without becoming any of them.
  </p>

  <p>
    This is partnership, not provision. A relationship with structure, not a
    service with scripts. A place where identity, experience, and direction can
    be explored without the constraints of a medical model, the performance of
    coaching, or the asymmetry of consultancy.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
